  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What runs, and when",
      "items": [
        "Every batch step is a GitHub Actions runner: nothing is always on doing the pipeline",
        "ingest at 06:00 daily, then transform, then image and pages, then deploy",
        "Azure runs only the API, at zero replicas until a request arrives",
        "The page ships no server at all: DuckDB compiled to WASM queries Parquet in the browser"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Who owns the running app",
      "items": [
        "Terraform owns the resource group, the environment and the container app, and ignores the image",
        "The deploy workflow owns the image and touches nothing else",
        "So a daily data refresh can never alter infrastructure"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Why the registry is GHCR",
      "items": [
        "Azure Container Registry has no free tier and bills per day whether or not anything is pulled",
        "The build has to happen in Actions anyway: the bucket key is mounted as a BuildKit secret",
        "That keeps the credential in one layer and recorded in none"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Credentials in play",
      "items": [
        "Terraform writes the scoped B2 key and the SEC contact address as Actions secrets; ingest, transform, image and pages all read them",
        "Azure needs no stored secret: deploy exchanges its own OIDC token for an Azure one at run time",
        "The GHCR pull token is the one long lived credential left, and it expires"
      ]
    }
  ]
}